# Business Constants Policy

Before introducing any string literal for a **reusable business value**, follow this order:

1. **Search** the repo for an existing constant (domain `constants.ts`, `catalogLabels.ts`, `@ob-cms/shared`, etc.).
2. **Reuse** it if it already exists.
3. **Create** a shared constant only when the same value appears in **2+ places** or defines a cross-module contract (queue names, webhook events, API labels).
4. **Never duplicate** label mappings (`Record<kind, label>`, status badges, filter chip text).
5. Prefer **enums / const objects / named exports** over inline strings.

## What must use constants

- UI labels, placeholders, tabs, badges, button text (when reused)
- Template kind labels and search labels
- Sort/filter option labels shared across surfaces
- Queue names, Bull prefix, cache key prefixes, webhook event names
- Permission/role identifiers (already in `@ob-cms/shared`)
- Error codes and provider identifiers when repeated

## What stays inline

- One-off copy (unique dialog body, single empty-state sentence with dynamic parts)
- User-generated content
- Craft block type names and schema identifiers tied to a single call site
- Test fixture descriptions that mirror production constants (import the constant when asserting)

## File placement

- Keep constants **close to their domain** (`views/template-library/constants.ts`, `template-catalog/lib/catalogLabels.ts`, `packages/shared/src/webhook-events.ts`).
- Avoid a single global constants dump; split by feature/package.
- Re-export from `@ob-cms/shared` only for values shared across apps (API, worker, admin, renderer).

## Examples in this repo

| Domain | Source |
|--------|--------|
| Template kind labels | `apps/admin/src/views/template-library/constants.ts` |
| Starter catalog labels | `apps/admin/src/views/template-catalog/lib/catalogLabels.ts` |
| Workflow state labels | `apps/admin/src/components/workflow/workflow.tsx` (`WORKFLOW_LABELS`) |
| Webhook events | `packages/shared/src/webhook-events.ts` |
| Bull prefix | `packages/shared/src/bull.constants.ts` |

When touching UI or infrastructure strings, ask: *"Could this drift if copied?"* If yes, centralize it.
